Here is a PyQt5 program that creates a window with a "Start" button which displays a message when clicked:

```python
import sys
from PyQt5.QtGui import QPushButton, QMessageBox

class TSTPDeepSeekHelper:
    def __init__(self):
        # Create the main window
        self.window = QMainWindow()
        self.window.setWindowTitle("TSTP DeepSeek Helper")
        
        # Create and center the button
        self.button = QPushButton("Start")
        self.button.setText("Start")
        self.button.clicked.connect(self.show_message)
        
        # Add the button to the window
        self.window.addWidget(self.button)
        
        # Center the window on the screen
        self.window.move((self.window screened.width() // 2), (self.window screenHeight() // 2))
        
    def show_message(self):
        QMessageBox.information(
            None,
            "TSTP DeepSeek Helper",
            "The helper is active!",
            QMessageBox.OK
        )

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app = QApplication(sys.argv)
    TSTPDeepSeekHelper().window.show()
    sys.exit(app.exec())
```

This program does the following:
1. Creates a main window with the title "TSTP DeepSeek Helper"
2. Adds a button labeled "Start" to the window
3. The button, when clicked, displays an information message using QMessageBox
4. The window is centered on the screen

When you run this program, it will show a simple window with a Start button that prints the message when clicked.

Note: Make sure you have PyQt5 installed in your Python environment for this to work. You can install it using pip if needed:

```bash
pip install PyQt5
```
