```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Hello World</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }

        #content {
            text-align: center;
        }

        .button {
            padding: 20px 30px;
            font-size: 24px;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: transform 0.3s ease;
        }

        .button:hover {
            transform: scale(1.1);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div #content>
        Hello World!
    </div>

    <button class="button" onclick="showEffect()">Click Me!</button>

    <script>
        function showEffect() {
            const content = document.getElementById('content');
            
            // Show the content with a delay
            setTimeout(() => {
                content.style.display = 'block';
                setTimeout(() => {
                    content.style.display = 'none';
                }, 3000 * Math.random() * (1000 - Math.random()) * 50); // Random animation duration between 1s and 5s
            }, 2000);
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates:

1. A simple HTML structure with a title, content div for the "Hello World" text, and a button.

2. CSS styling that:
   - Makes the body take up the full viewport height
   - Centers the content vertically
   - Styles the button to look clickable (with hover scaling)
   - Centers everything horizontally

3. JavaScript:
   - A `showEffect` function that shows/hides the "Hello World" text
   - Uses `setTimeout` for both showing and hiding
   - The hide animation has a random duration between 1 second and 5 seconds with some variation
   - The button has hover scaling effect

When you click the button, it will:
- Show "Hello World" after 2 seconds (randomly delayed)
- Then hide it after a random number of seconds between 1 and 5 seconds

The text will appear to fade in and out with a smooth animation. The button also scales slightly when hovered over.

You can save this code in an HTML file and open it in a web browser to see the effect in action.
