Here's a simple example website for a fake Detroit mechanic shop:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Detroit Mechanic Shop</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .shop-container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
        }

        .shop-header {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 40px 0;
        }

        .shop-name {
            font-size: 2.5em;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            color: #2c3e50;
        }

        .featured-section {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 40px;
            margin-top: -40px; /* Hidden on mobile */
        }

        .mechanic-card {
            background: #f4f6f9;
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 20px;
            width: 300px;
            text-align: center;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        .mechanic-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-5px);
            box-shadow: 0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
        }

        .mechanic-image {
            width: 100%;
            height: 200px;
            object-fit: cover;
            border-radius: 10px 10px 0 0;
        }

        .mechanic-info {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .price {
            font-size: 1.5em;
            font-weight: bold;
            color: #2c3e50;
        }

        /* Responsive design */
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .shop-header {
                padding: 20px;
            }
            
            .featured-section {
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 20px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="shop-container">
        <div class="shop-header">
            <h1 class="shop-name">Tech Reps Inc.</h1>
            <p>Quality repairs done right in Detroit</p>
        </div>

        <div class="featured-section">
            <div class="mechanic-card">
                <img src="https://picsum.photos/500/300" alt="Mechanic 1" class="mechanic-image">
                <div class="mechanic-info">
                    <p>Alex Smith</p>
                    <p>Master Mechanic</p>
                    <p class="price">$125/hour</p>
                </div>
                <button onclick="bookNow(1)">Book Now</button>
            </div>

            <div class="mechanic-card">
                <img src="https://picsum.photos/501/301" alt="Mechanic 2" class="mechanic-image">
                <div class="mechanic-info">
                    <p>Emily Rodriguez</p>
                    <p>Certified Tech</p>
                    <p class="price">$99/hour</p>
                </div>
                <button onclick="bookNow(2)">Book Now</button>
            </div>

            <div class="mechanic-card">
                <img src="https://picsum.photos/502/302" alt="Mechanic 3" class="mechanic-image">
                <div class="mechanic-info">
                    <p>Jason Johnson</p>
                    <p>Experienced Mechanic</p>
                    <p class="price">$150/hour</p>
                </div>
                <button onclick="bookNow(3)">Book Now</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function bookNow(index) {
            document.querySelectorAll('.mechanic-card').forEach(card => {
                card.style.transform = `scale(${index === parseInt(card.querySelector('.mechanic-number')) ? 1.3 : 0.8})`;
            });
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This example includes:

1. Responsive design with grid layout
2. Hover effects on mechanic cards
3. Smooth transitions
4. Box shadows for depth
5. Grid and flexbox layouts
6. Simple JavaScript interaction
7. Proper spacing and padding
8. Border radius effects
9. Mock images and details

Features:
- Shop header with name and tagline
- Featured section with three mechanic cards
- Each card has:
  - Image placeholder
  - Mechanic's name and title
  - Price
  - "Book Now" button
- Responsive design that works on mobile devices
- Hover animations
- Shadow effects for depth

You can customize the colors, spacing, and other properties by modifying the CSS variables in the style section. The JavaScript is minimal for now but you could add more functionality like appointment scheduling or customer interactions later.

To use this, just save it as an HTML file and open it in a web browser. Make sure you have internet connection if you want to replace the placeholder images with real ones.
