For styling, I want the site to look old-school, so I'll use a dark background with amber text. Using flexbox can help center the content both vertically and horizontally. I'll create classes for the shop name, description, hours, contact info, and schedule. Each section will be in its own div with appropriate padding and margins for spacing.

The JavaScript part is minimal because the user didn't ask for dynamic features. Maybe a button to show/hide the schedule or an animation when clicking on the shop name. I'll keep it simple, adding a hover effect on the button.

