Here's a simple example website for a fake mechanic shop in Detroit:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>DTW Mechanic Shop - Fake but Close to Accurate</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
        }

        body {
            background-color: #2c3e50;
            color: #ecf0f1;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .shop-name {
            font-size: 3em;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            text-align: center;
            text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        }

        .content {
            flex-grow: 1;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
        }

        .shop-description {
            font-size: 1.2em;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        .shop-hours {
            list-style-type:bullet;
            padding: 0;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .shop-hours li {
            margin: 0 20px;
        }

        .contact-info {
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            font-size: 1.2em;
        }

        .schedule {
            border-top: 1px solid #cdc7b6;
            padding: 10px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        button {
            background-color: #dc3545;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            font-size: 1.1em;
            cursor: pointer;
            border-radius: 5px;
            margin-top: 10px;
        }

        button:hover {
            opacity: 0.9;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1 class="shop-name">DTW Mechanic Shop</h1>
    
    <div class="content">
        <p class="shop-description">
            Welcome to the official online directory of theDTW Mechanic Shop, your trusted partner in Detroit's mechanical excellence.
            We specialize in classic car maintenance, rare engine rebuilds, and all-around automotive expertise.
            Our team of skilled mechanics has years of experience working on old-school vehicles from across North America.
        </p>

        <div class="shop-hours">
            <strong>Opening Hours</strong>
            <br>
            <ul class="shop-hours">
                <li>Monday - Saturday: 8 AM - 6 PM</li>
                <li>Sunday: Closed</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <p class="contact-info">
            Contact us for all your classic car needs:
            <br>
            <em>Email: raremech@dtw.com</em>
            <br>
            <em>Phone: (555) 123-4567</em>
            <br>
            <em>Address: 123 Auto Lane, Detroit, MI 48201</em>
        </p>

        <div class="schedule">
            <h3>Schedule Overview</h3>
            <div style="border-top: 1px solid #cdc7b6; gap: 10px;">
                <!-- Repeat this block for multiple schedule entries -->
                <div style="text-align: center; margin: 20px 0;">Monday, Next Available at 9 AM</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <button onclick="toggle Schedule">Show Schedule</button>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

This example includes:

1. A dark theme with amber accents (typical of old Detroit aesthetic)
2. Responsive layout using flexbox
3. Proper spacing between elements using margin and padding
4. Border styling for the schedule section
5. A simple JavaScript feature to toggle the visibility of the schedule (you can modify this based on your needs)

Features:
- Fake shop name and description
- Realistic opening hours format
- Contact information with realistic email and phone number
- Schedule display with a border
- Toggle button for the schedule

To use this template:

1. Copy the code into an HTML file
