Here's a Python script that creates and displays a pop-up message using Tkinter:

```python
import tkinter as tk

def show_pop_up():
    root = tk.Tk()
    root.title("Click Here")
    
    frame = tk.Frame(root)
    frame.grid_configure(row=0, column=0, sticky='NEWS')  # Sticks to center position
    
    label = tk.Label(frame, text="Click Here", bg="white", fg="black")
    label.pack(anchor='center')
    
    root.mainloop()
```

You can save this script as a `.py` file and run it in your computer's terminal. The pop-up will appear centered on your screen.

When you open the script:
1. It creates a new Tkinter window.
2. Sets the window title to "Click Here".
3. Creates a frame to position the message.
4. Adds a label with the message text and sets its background to white.
5. Positions the label in the center of the screen using grid geometry manager.
6. Starts the main loop.

The pop-up will appear centered on your screen when you run the script, and it can be closed by clicking anywhere outside of it or closing the window manually.
